From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: OpenBook <noreply@anybook.invalid>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] OPENBOOK: Launcher3 may start contextual search

ContextualSearchInvoker calls ContextualSearchManager.startContextualSearch()
for the pointer shake (SystemUI's contextual cursor), Meta+A and Meta+G, all
of which SystemUI hands to Launcher3 through invokeContextualSearch(). The
service requires ACCESS_CONTEXTUAL_SEARCH (signature|privileged), which
AOSP's Launcher3QuickStep does not request, so every such call failed:

  SecurityException: Permission Denial: Cannot call startContextualSearch
  from pid=0, uid=10092

Request it. Launcher3QuickStep is not platform-signed, so the device's
privapp allowlist must grant it too (OpenBook does, next to its contextual
search app).
---
 quickstep/AndroidManifest.xml | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/quickstep/AndroidManifest.xml b/quickstep/AndroidManifest.xml
index 789e0a5263..7c07a4dc41 100644
--- a/quickstep/AndroidManifest.xml
+++ b/quickstep/AndroidManifest.xml
@@ -59,6 +59,9 @@
     -->
     <uses-permission android:name="android.permission.ACCESS_HIDDEN_PROFILES_FULL" />
 
+    <!-- Start contextual search: the pointer shake, Meta+A and Meta+G (OPENBOOK). -->
+    <uses-permission android:name="android.permission.ACCESS_CONTEXTUAL_SEARCH" />
+
     <!-- Permission required to listen to recent, all app key gestures. -->
     <uses-permission android:name="android.permission.MANAGE_KEY_GESTURES"
         android:featureFlag="com.android.window.flags.grant_manage_key_gestures_to_recents" />
